author ai
group gui/graph
note Where every node on the canvas ends up. The layout is a forest of compact subtrees, recomputed from scratch every frame by Built::place_nodes; a node the reader dragged then has its position overwritten by the dragged one (App::graph_layout, in graph-draw). Horizontally a node's column is its Rank - its depth in the path tree, or one rank out from whatever expansion revealed it - and the columns are placed outward from rank 0 so the root of the path never moves. Vertically each node owns a block as tall as itself or as the stack of its children's blocks, whichever is more, and centres in it; sibling blocks never interleave, so a wide subtree only pushes its own siblings around. A final sweep separates the rare collisions between different subtrees that land in the same column. Everything is in cells and rows (theme::Cells), which no zoom changes; pixels appear only when a rectangle is asked for with this frame's cell size.

